Subject: [PATCH] pygnmi: support double_val in subscription updates

Backport https://github.com/akarneliuk/pygnmi/pull/165, missing from the
PyPI 0.8.15 artifacts. Preserve double-valued telemetry, including zero.

Related: https://github.com/akarneliuk/pygnmi/issues/179
Revalidate/remove when upgrading the pinned dependency to a corrected release.
---
 pygnmi/client.py | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pygnmi/client.py b/pygnmi/client.py
--- a/pygnmi/client.py
+++ b/pygnmi/client.py
@@ -1329,6 +1329,9 @@ def telemetryParser(in_message=None, debug: bool = False):
                     elif update_msg.val.HasField("float_val"):
                         update_container.update({"val": update_msg.val.float_val})

+                    elif update_msg.val.HasField("double_val"):
+                        update_container.update({"val": update_msg.val.double_val})
+
                     elif update_msg.val.HasField("decimal_val"):
                         update_container.update({"val": update_msg.val.decimal_val})
